==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*hairaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*kei-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*koi-}}. Cognate with {{cog|goh|hēr}} ({{cog|de|hehr||august, holy}}), {{cog|non|hárr||grey}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌹𐍃||torch}}, {{cog|osx|hēr}}. Non-Germanic cognates include {{cog|sa|केतु|tr=ketu||light, torch}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hɑːɹ/|lang=ang}}

===Adjective===
{{ang-adj|head=hār}}

# Grey-haired, [[old]] and [[grey]], [[venerable]].

